{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Who sends.</b> He whose practice is to send emissaries by sea." "<b>Go.</b> You swift messengers, and bear tidings to Israel who fled and were exiled, and they are beyond the rivers of Cush." "And on account of the rivers he said, \"and in vessels of papyrus.\"" "<b>Drawn away.</b> They are Israel, who were dragged from their place like sheep until they were scraped bare." "<b>Drawn away to a nation feared.</b> They are the Cushites." "<b>From it [הוא].</b> From that people, or it is a hint to the rivers." "<b>A nation, etc.</b> His intention was like the intention of a child when he is taught line upon line; therefore it was despised." "And the alef of <b>bazav</b> is for the lack of the doubled letter, and like it דליו שוקים (Proverbs 26:7), according to the opinion of R. Moses the Cohen." "And the meaning of <b>rivers</b> is kings, like \"the waters of the river\" (Isaiah 8:7)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {7 "Reading בזאו against the lemma form בזוו possibly implied by the comment about missing doubling; translating the form as it appears in the Hebrew comment."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:13.184680387Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}